Third-party software in the smock binary
========================================

The smock binary, both the release binaries and the one in the container
image, is built with the MoonBit toolchain moonc v0.10.14+7d59c7ec9, which
smock --version names. The software below is compiled or linked into it.
Each part stays under its own licence. Where that is the Apache License,
Version 2.0, its text is the one in LICENSE.

- moonbitlang/core: Apache License, Version 2.0
- moonbitlang/async: Apache License, Version 2.0
- moonbitlang/x: Apache License, Version 2.0
- The MoonBit native runtime: Apache License, Version 2.0
- mimalloc: MIT License
- simdutf: MIT License
- Data from the Unicode Character Database 18.0.0: Unicode License v3

smock links OpenSSL 3 and the GNU C Library dynamically, so they are not
part of the binary. In the container image they come from its distroless
base, which keeps their copyright files under /usr/share/doc.


